{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"**Yes.** Under the Central Bank of Ireland’s UCITS Q&A 1088, a fund may have both listed ETF share classes and unlisted share classes. The prospectus should clearly compare the classes’ **dealing arrangements, settlement arrangements, costs, minimum subscription amounts, rights, liquidity and pricing**.\n\nThis is the Irish disclosure point; it does not import US share-class exemptive conditions."}}
